I don't quite like it coming to a full halt
anywhere, that just doesn't seem right, somehow,
that the player gets _nothing_ for a kill.

I posted somewhere else, who knows where by now, a
proposal that the score per monster killed of each
type converge, independently per type, slowly or
quickly to 1, per kill, perhaps scores for nastier
monsters decaying faster, thus making billion point
scores conceptually possible, but no longer
physically possible. That this breaks save file
compatibility is perhaps avoidable (since the kill
counts per type are known and saved, recalculation
of the current score per beast killed is possible),
but also perhaps too much work.

I also objected that holding down monster scoring
benefits those who _want_ low XLs, though it isn't
the case that score and XP need to remain coupled,
I guess.

That doesn't have much bearing on a particular
proposal to slam kill scoring shut at some high XL's
worth, though, just on score-for-kill suppression in
general.

